$ Milestone 6, spec §23: num()/dec()/tex() casts. Covers every accepted
$ source tag for each cast (num/dec/yn/tex, per runtime/cast.c's design
$ note), including truncation-toward-zero for dec->num and tex parsing
$ with surrounding whitespace tolerated.

show(num(3.9))
show(num(-3.9))
show(num(Yes))
show(num(No))
show(num("42"))
show(num("  -7  "))

show(dec(5))
show(dec(Yes))
show(dec("3.5"))

show(tex(5))
show(tex(3.25))
show(tex(Yes))
show(tex([1, 2, 3]))

$ Round-trips and a small computation to prove the cast result is a real,
$ usable value of the target type, not just printable.
x = num("10") + num("32")
show(x)
y = dec("1.5") * 4
show(y)

$ Casts are ordinary runtime errors, catchable with do/grabe just like any
$ other Fly error (milestone 5). Note: per genDoGrabe's documented MVP
$ limitation (codegen.cpp, milestone 5 -- "does NOT run ARC cleanup for
$ ... locals that are live ... at the moment of unwind"), the tex literal
$ argument below is a live temporary at the instant num() throws, so this
$ one case leaks that one small allocation under valgrind -- a known,
$ already-documented gap in the unwind path, not a new bug in casting
$ itself (arithmetic/comparison errors thrown with only num/dec operands,
$ as in examples/error_handling.fly, don't hit it, since there's no heap
$ temp live at the throw point in those cases).
do {
    show(num("not a number"))
} grabe (e) {
    show(e)
}
